// The likeness of photos (dHash) on a reference set from Pillow: three photo-like frames of 384 by
// 288 (light falling across, shapes, a blur, grain), each as a JPEG of quality 95, 75 and 50 and
// reduced to a half and a third (quality 85). The frames are the hardest of twenty such sets
// measured for E5i: frame a holds the farthest copies (16 bits apart, a half against quality 95),
// frames b and c the nearest strangers (19 bits). Over the twenty sets copies lay 0 to 16 bits
// apart and strangers 19 to 44, which is where the thresholds come from. The samples are in base64,
// each cut into pieces a compiler of Windows takes as one literal.

